# Declared VS Code extensions. Applied by script/vscode-extensions.
#
# Format: publisher.name@version  # what it does and why it is here
#
# Every entry carries an EXACT version. An extension is unreviewed third-party
# code running inside the editor with the editor's filesystem access, so it gets
# the same treatment as an MCP server package in ADR-029: no floating versions,
# no implicit latest. See ADR-032.
#
# Pinning only means something while VS Code's own extension auto-update is off.
# `script/vscode-extensions --verify` reports drift either way, and warns when
# that setting would defeat the pins.
#
# ONLY ROOTS ARE DECLARED. An extension pack or dependency installs its children
# automatically, and pinning a child here would add a version that moves on its
# own schedule for no benefit. `--diff` resolves pack membership from the
# installed extensions on disk, so children are not reported as undeclared.
# The children currently arriving this way are named in the comments below.
#
# Ids are case-sensitive as published — golang.Go, EditorConfig.EditorConfig —
# even though `code --install-extension` matches without regard to case.

# --- AI coding agents ---------------------------------------------------------
# All three send file contents to a remote service by design. That is their
# purpose and it is a deliberate choice, but it is the widest data path in this
# file, so it is stated rather than left implicit.
anthropic.claude-code@2.1.237  # Editor integration for the Claude Code CLI in dev.Brewfile.
openai.chatgpt@26.5818.21641   # Codex, OpenAI's coding agent; pairs with the codex cask.
saoudrizwan.claude-dev@4.1.10  # Cline; pairs with the npm:cline CLI in mise's config. Not the deprecated brew formula (ADR-044).

# --- Remote and container development ----------------------------------------
ms-vscode-remote.remote-containers@0.467.0    # Devcontainer client; the reason dev.Brewfile installs VS Code.
ms-vscode-remote.remote-ssh@0.125.2026081318  # Edit over SSH on Lima VMs and remote hosts. Pack: adds remote-ssh-edit and ms-vscode.remote-explorer.
ms-azuretools.vscode-docker@2.0.0             # Dockerfile and Compose editing. Depends on ms-azuretools.vscode-containers, which does the work since 2.0.

# --- Kubernetes ---------------------------------------------------------------
ms-kubernetes-tools.vscode-kubernetes-tools@1.4.1 # Manifest authoring and cluster browsing. Depends on redhat.vscode-yaml, which is also declared below in its own right.

# --- Languages ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The toolchains themselves come from mise (ADR-021); these are the editor half.
golang.Go@0.57.2                     # Go language support.
ms-python.python@2026.7.2026080801   # Python language support. Pack: adds vscode-pylance, debugpy and vscode-python-envs.
ms-toolsai.jupyter@2026.6.2026071501 # Notebooks, including MLX experiments. Pack: adds jupyter-keymap, jupyter-renderers, vscode-jupyter-cell-tags and vscode-jupyter-slideshow.
dbaeumer.vscode-eslint@3.0.34        # JavaScript and TypeScript linting.
esbenp.prettier-vscode@12.4.0        # Formatter for web and Markdown files.

# --- Markup and data ----------------------------------------------------------
redhat.vscode-yaml@1.25.2026082008 # YAML validation and schema completion for workflows and manifests.
redhat.vscode-xml@0.29.2026081308  # XML and XSD editing.

# --- Build and version control ------------------------------------------------
ms-vscode.makefile-tools@0.13.37 # Makefile targets; this repository uses just, other projects use make.
eamodio.gitlens@2026.8.190513    # Blame, history and range navigation. Prompts for a GitKraken account for its paid features; the free feature set needs no sign-in.

# --- Appearance ---------------------------------------------------------------
vscode-icons-team.vscode-icons@12.19.0 # File-explorer icons. Independent of the terminal Nerd Font glyphs.

# --- Recommended, not installed ----------------------------------------------
# These mirror gates that ./script/test already runs, so enabling them makes the
# editor agree with CI instead of adding new capability. Uncomment to adopt.
#timonwong.shellcheck@0.39.5            # The same shellcheck the test suite runs, inline while editing.
#foxundermoon.shell-format@7.2.8        # shfmt formatting, matching tests/format.sh.
#tamasfe.even-better-toml@0.21.2        # TOML editing; chezmoi, mise, starship and atuin configs are all TOML.
#EditorConfig.EditorConfig@0.18.2       # Applies the repository .editorconfig rather than personal defaults.
#DavidAnson.vscode-markdownlint@0.62.1  # Markdown linting for a documentation-heavy repository.

# --- Further alternatives -----------------------------------------------------
#HashiCorp.terraform@2.40.0    # HCL for the `cloud` profile's OpenTofu.
#charliermarsh.ruff@2026.72.0  # Ruff linting and formatting for Python.
#rust-lang.rust-analyzer@0.4.3020 # Rust language server.
